BonVoyage API Gateway native packaging
==================================

This package contains the gateway executable and its hardened systemd unit.
It supplies neither a snapshot, secrets, control-plane process nor tuning.
Install a reviewed snapshot at /etc/bonvoyage/snapshot.pb (root:bonvoyage 0640).
After verifying configuration and dependencies, explicitly enable/start
bonvoyage.service. Admin and metrics endpoints remain bound to loopback.

Runtime logger severity is sent through the local syslog socket to journald.
Raw stdout/stderr are retained at info priority without interpreting <N>
prefixes. Ensure /dev/log and journald are available before starting; no
fallback delivery, remote delivery or unlimited retention is guaranteed.
The package never changes host-wide journald, rsyslog or wall policy.

Upgrades stop the service and do not start it again automatically. Perform
upgrades in a reviewed maintenance window, verify the package and snapshot,
then explicitly start the service. Keep the prior package for rollback.

Removal/purge retains service identity, snapshots, secrets, state and logs.
No installer recursively removes operator data or changes CPU/NIC/IRQ policy.
The source-install unit in /etc/systemd/system must be reconciled before
installation; this package never silently replaces that administrator unit.

The current experimental tuning adapter supports only the separately accepted
/usr/local source-install contract, not this package's /usr/bin unit. Package
installation does not grant tuning or benchmark qualification.

Private rehearsal builds are not signed public releases or OSS license grants.
